{
  "text": "Based on the search results, I can provide you with the current Node.js LTS version information:\n\n## Current Node.js LTS Version: **Node.js 24** (Codename: Krypton)\n\nNode.js 24 is the current active LTS line in June 2026. For production applications that require stability, Node.js 24 is the current Active LTS release and Node.js 22 is in Maintenance LTS.\n\n### Other Supported Versions:\n\n- **Node.js 22** (Codename: Jod) - Currently in Maintenance LTS phase, supported through April 2027\n- **Node.js 20** (Codename: Iron) - Also in Maintenance LTS\n- **Node.js 26** - Currently in the Current (non-LTS) phase until October 2026, when it will transition to Active LTS\n\n### Recommendation:\n\nUse Node 24 for new projects. It provides the best balance of stability, long-term support, and modern features for production applications as of September 2026.",
